{"name":"Mountain Peak","hex":"#e9e0d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elevation of land of considerable dimensions rising more or less abruptly, forming a conspicuous figure in the landscape, usually having a small extent of surface at its summit. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something very large in size or quantity; a huge amount; a great heap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain"},{"term":"peak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A point; the sharp end or top of anything that terminates in a point; as, the peak, or front, of a cap.","The highest value reached by some quantity in a time period."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To raise the point of (a gaff) closer to perpendicular.","To raise an oar out of the water, fitting the handle into a round slot or socket located at the bottom of the boat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peak"}],"entries":[{"title":"Summit","blocks":[{"text":"A summit is a point on a surface that is higher in elevation than all points immediately adjacent to it. The topographic terms acme, apex, peak, and zenith are synonymous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Summitting_Island_Peak.jpg/330px-Summitting_Island_Peak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summit","wikidata":"Q207326"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain","wikidata":"Q8502"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Monte_Rosa_summit.jpg/500px-Monte_Rosa_summit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Monte_Rosa_summit.jpg/1280px-Monte_Rosa_summit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Monte_Rosa_summit.jpg/500px-Monte_Rosa_summit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View from the summit of Switzerland's highest peak, Monte Rosa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonte_Rosa_summit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/SiskiyouSummit.jpg/500px-SiskiyouSummit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/SiskiyouSummit.jpg/1280px-SiskiyouSummit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/SiskiyouSummit.jpg/500px-SiskiyouSummit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Siskiyou Mountain Summit sign along Interstate 5 in Oregon, marking the highest point along the highway at 4,310 ft (1,310 m)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASiskiyouSummit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Damavand-Iran-2018.jpg/500px-Damavand-Iran-2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa